      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nRegression coverage for the aiter ungrouped-router shared-expert slot accounting\r\nfixed in #40943. The failure mode this locks down is silent: the routed/shared\r\nsplit can be wrong while the final `topk_ids` width stays correct, so nothing\r\nraises and only the routing quality degrades. \r\n\r\nThis surfaced while tuning MiniMax-M3 for **vision-language serving**, where\r\nthe shared-expert fusion path is on the per-token decode path of an\r\nimage-conditioned workload. \r\n\r\n## What this does\r\n\r\nThe gate stand-in `_fake_gate` encodes `moe_fused_gate`'s real width contract\r\n(K = total topk columns, last `num_fused_shared_experts` of them filled with\r\n`num_experts + (slot - K_routed)`), including the `topk > num_shared` assertion,\r\nso the fake cannot drift into being more permissive than the kernel.\r\n\r\nRuns on any host: the append path reads only `num_fused_shared_experts` and\r\n`_use_aiter`, so `_use_aiter` is patched on and `_is_cpu` off (the only gate on\r\nthe JIT gate dispatch). Registered CPU-only, no accelerator required.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n`python -m pytest test/registered/unit/layers/moe/test_aiter_fused_shared_experts_append.py`\r\n— 1 passed locally on CPU, against current upstream `main`, i.e. against the\r\nshipped fix rather than a local variant of it.\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38378140075](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38378140075)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38378139400](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38378139400)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38378139708](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38378139708)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\r\n",
